WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.525 --> 00:00:01.648
- [Narrator] Ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:01.648 --> 00:00:03.395
we all know that the
American flag has endured,

00:00:03.395 --> 00:00:04.732
in its many forms,

00:00:04.732 --> 00:00:07.029
as the ultimate symbol
of freedom, justice,

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:08.050
and the American way,

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.776
but did you know that our nation's flag

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:13.323
was designed by a high
school student from Ohio?

00:00:13.323 --> 00:00:15.797
("Yankee Doodle Dandy")

00:00:15.797 --> 00:00:18.041
- [Narrator] According to legend,
the original American flag

00:00:18.041 --> 00:00:21.447
from 1776 was sewn by a
lady named Betsy Ross.

00:00:21.447 --> 00:00:24.712
It had 13 stars in a circle
representing America's

00:00:24.712 --> 00:00:26.348
original 13 states.

00:00:26.348 --> 00:00:28.130
As more states joined the union,

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.603
people kept adding more stars to the flag,

00:00:30.603 --> 00:00:34.299
so by 1958 the US flag
had a total of 48 stars

00:00:34.299 --> 00:00:36.313
for the 48 states of that time.

00:00:36.313 --> 00:00:39.104
Which brings us to our high
school student, Robert Heft.

00:00:39.104 --> 00:00:41.643
Robert's history teacher gave his students

00:00:41.643 --> 00:00:43.508
an open-ended assignment.

00:00:43.508 --> 00:00:45.546
"Make a project illustrating

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:46.903
"your interest in American history.

00:00:46.903 --> 00:00:48.075
"It could be anything."

00:00:48.075 --> 00:00:51.135
So, Robert, who was jazzed
about hearing that Alaska

00:00:51.135 --> 00:00:52.888
and Hawaii were going to become states,

00:00:52.888 --> 00:00:56.237
cut up an old 48 state flag
in his grandparents' basement

00:00:56.237 --> 00:01:00.237
and designed his own
vision for a 50 state flag.

00:01:01.306 --> 00:01:02.804
When he turned his final assignment,

00:01:02.804 --> 00:01:05.934
Robert's teacher said,
"Anyone can make a flag,

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.800
"and it's got the wrong number of stars."

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.686
The grade came back a B minus.

00:01:10.686 --> 00:01:14.184
Robert tried to explain his idea
to his teacher who replied,

00:01:14.184 --> 00:01:16.674
"I'll change your grade
when your flag is accepted

00:01:16.674 --> 00:01:18.492
"by the US Congress."

00:01:18.492 --> 00:01:19.325
Game on.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:23.600
Robert wrote 21 letters
and called The White House

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:28.286
18 times until one day in
1960, Robert's phone rang.

00:01:28.286 --> 00:01:29.933
(phone rings)

00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:30.812
- [Robert] Hello?

00:01:30.812 --> 00:01:31.934
- [President Eisenhower]
Hello, Robert Heft?

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.223
- [Narrator] It was President Eisenhower

00:01:33.223 --> 00:01:35.346
with news that Robert's
50 state flag design

00:01:35.346 --> 00:01:38.420
had actually been chosen
as the new official flag

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.153
of the United States.

00:01:40.153 --> 00:01:42.892
The President invited Robert
to Washington where he saw

00:01:42.892 --> 00:01:47.059
his American flag fly for the
first time on July 4th, 1960.

00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:53.579
Since then, Robert's 50 state
flag has remained unmatched

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:56.417
as the quintessential symbol of America.

00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:57.755
But I know what you're thinking,

00:01:57.755 --> 00:02:00.694
whatever happened to that B minus?

00:02:00.694 --> 00:02:02.489
Robert's teacher honored his promise

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.989
and changed the grade to an A.

